1. Scope

This licence applies only to original VIGIL OS source, documentation and
branding owned by Brad Heffernan for which he can grant these terms, and only
to the extent that no applicable third-party or copyleft licence governs
that material. This eligible original material is the Covered Material.

Covered Material includes eligible original build code and desktop defaults,
and eligible original VIGIL names, logos, wallpapers and other artwork.
The project includes other material to which these terms do not apply.
Section 5 defines the exclusions and takes precedence over any restriction
in this licence. File-specific notices and provenance must be retained.

2. Personal build permission

You may view, download and clone the repository, and build, install and run
an unmodified copy of the Covered Material for your own noncommercial use.
You may share an exact unmodified source copy without payment or profit if
you retain this licence, all required notices and the complete branding.
No permission to redistribute Covered Material in binary images is granted
by this licence; obtain separate written permission from the copyright owner.

The supplied build pipeline may generate or transform build outputs,
resize artwork without changing its design, and increment version metadata.
You may select its documented edition, workspace, cache and output options
and edit the documented version.json build number, codename and counter.
These mechanical build and configuration actions are permitted exceptions
to the unmodified-copy requirement. They do not permit removal or redesign
of the branding, changes to product code or reuse in another project.

